  "configuration_id": "config_035",
  "reason": "All nine completed experiments use multiprofile, so the value of multiprofile versus singleprofile is entirely untested. The strongest configuration so far is config_007 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile) at 0.706 acc. config_035 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l, singleprofile, weighted) changes only the profile setting relative to config_007 (aggregation becomes None as a natural consequence of single-profile), giving a clean A/B test of whether multiprofile aggregation contributes meaningfully. If singleprofile matches or approaches 0.706, it simplifies the pipeline and redirects future effort; if it falls well short, it confirms multiprofile is a critical design choice and justifies further multiprofile-specific tuning. Under a limited budget, resolving this high-level architectural question is more informative than fine-tuning fusion or aggregation within an already well-supported multiprofile setting."
}

